---
import Simple from '../layouts/Simple.astro';
import { site, ub } from '../data/site.js';
---
<Simple
  schema={{ '@type': 'AboutPage', name: 'About prewarmed.org', url: 'https://prewarmed.org/about/', publisher: { '@id': 'https://prewarmed.org/#org' } }}
  title="About prewarmed.org"
  description="Who runs prewarmed.org, how it relates to Warm Inboxes, Upscale B2B and Alpha Forge, how the site is funded, and why that is stated on every page."
  eyebrow="About"
  h1="Who runs this"
  lede="No mystery, and no pretence of independence we have not earned.">
  <p class="note">{site.disclosure}</p>
  <h2>Why this site exists separately</h2>
  <p>Most of what is written about prewarmed infrastructure is written by people selling it, with no numbers attached, and most of what is sold as prewarmed skips either the aging or the warming. This site exists to state a specific, checkable definition of the term and to document the checks a buyer can run themselves.</p>
  <p>We sell the thing we write about. That is stated on every page rather than buried, because a reader who discovers it later is entitled to feel handled, and one told up front is not.</p>
  <h2>What we operate</h2>
  <p>Warm Inboxes runs prewarmed and fresh Google Workspace, Microsoft 365 and Azure infrastructure, and sends at volume across its own campaigns. The figures and recommendations on this site come from operating that infrastructure.</p>
  <p>The same team runs <a href={ub('/', { page: 'about', placement: 'body' })} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Upscale B2B</a>, which runs cold email campaigns for clients end to end. That is where a lot of the sending behind these numbers actually happens, and it is why the advice here is written from the position of someone who has to live with the consequences of it.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If a number here is wrong, tell us at <a href={`mailto:${site.correctionsEmail}`}>{site.correctionsEmail}</a> and we will fix it and say what changed.</p>
</Simple>
